#* {{quote-book|en|year=1846| title=The National Portrait Gallery of Illustrious and Eminent Personages, Chiefly of the Nineteenth Century|author=William Cooke Taylor | page=34| passage=But though he thus abstained from power, his eldest son, the present Lord Morpeth, as Secretary for Ireland at a critical period, acquired a higher reputation and a more '''deserved''' popularity than any statesman who ever held that office.}}
